## 2.11 Correlation Matrix (Engagement Metrics)

|  | Likes | Shares | Comments | Total Engagement |
|--|-------|--------|----------|------------------|
| **Likes** | 1.000 | -0.001 | 0.010 | 0.911 |
| **Shares** | -0.001 | 1.000 | 0.024 | 0.336 |
| **Comments** | 0.010 | 0.024 | 1.000 | 0.179 |
| **Total Engagement** | 0.911 | 0.336 | 0.179 | 1.000 |

**Follower Count vs Total Engagement correlation**: **-0.011**

**Insight**: Likes, shares, and comments are **completely uncorrelated** with each other (r values near zero). This is atypical for organic social media where these metrics usually co-vary (a viral post gets more of everything). Likes dominate total engagement (r=0.911), while shares (r=0.336) and comments (r=0.179) contribute less. The near-zero follower-engagement correlation (-0.011) means **follower count does not predict engagement** -- the platform appears to reward content quality over audience size.

